{
  "note": "Hand-written cross-stack vectors for the guardian SCREEN_LOCK_RESET (kind 31122), spec/contract.md 'Screen-lock reset'. NOT generated by the scripts/ generators: edit by hand (a one-off script made the ciphertexts with nostr-tools' NIP-44 v2), keeping every consumer green. The guardian seals the PIN to the machine BEFORE signing: plaintext = the PIN as a JSON string (`plaintext`; \"\" removes the screen lock), sealed with NIP-44 v2 under conversation_key(ephemeralSecretKey, machine) with the vector's fixed `nonce`; `epk` is the ephemeral x-only pubkey. It then signs a NIP-01 inner event of `kind` with exactly `tags` and content = the compact JSON in `content` (field order v, id, machine, issuedAt, epk, newPinSealed; created_at = issuedAt), seals and gift-wraps it to the machine like a RELEASE. The secret keys here are TEST keys only. Rust consumers: core/crates/charter-verify/tests/screen_lock_reset_vectors.rs (shape, invalid, window), core/crates/charter-transport/tests/screen_lock_seal_vectors.rs (the seal opens to `newPin`, re-seals byte-identically, and every `sealFailures` case fails to open), android/jni (a ward holding `machineSecretKey` applies `vectors` and records `failed` for `sealFailures`). TS producer: apps/charter-app/src/wire/screenLockVectors.test.ts.",
